        "id": 128
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-06T10:03:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, in this case openstack-placement is like the -common subpackages are for other services holding \"common\" files for the different services that may exist, as config files, comon executables, etc... If so the common pattern is that services subpackages require the -common subpackage and deployers should explicitely install -api not the other way around. In this way, if in the future a new service is added to placement, we could modularly select the services to install and run on each case. Otherwise, there is no much point in creating a subpackage for -api. What do you think?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 49,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "223246f9ce10c59e3aa39ec10817694e5da9334c",
